(2653665, 368375, 16004, '<td valign="top">this is a lovely image, but the focus on the bee is just (noticably) a smidgeon too soft.  this is easily rectifiable with a mix of unsharp mask and sharpen edges.  given that he''s the main point of interest, i thik it would be worth doing.  other than that it''s really nice - the colours are rich and i feel suitably golden (albeit the flower is a touch orange) and the depth of field / bokeh has a really nice effect overall.  7.</td>', 'this is a lovely image, but the focus on the bee is just (noticably) a smidgeon too soft.  this is easily rectifiable with a mix of unsharp mask and sharpen edges.  given that he''s the main point of interest, i thik it would be worth doing.  other than that it''s really nice - the colours are rich and i feel suitably golden (albeit the flower is a touch orange) and the depth of field / bokeh has a really nice effect overall.  7.', '2006-07-24 03:40:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(2653669, 368359, 16241, '<td valign="top">best of k.m.  great shot</td>', 'best of k.m.  great shot', '2006-07-24 03:42:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(2653673, 366958, 16004, '<td valign="top">you will be punished for the size of the shot, and normally i would be band wagining and telling you to use save to web, or lower quality, or something to make saving it under the kb limit at full size.  but, oddly, the size of the shot for a change adds a degree of intimacy, and there is something tender about it.  i would imagine it would look good in a big frame...  anyway, technically i feel the sun is suffering from some colour abnormality on the left, and there is a bit of glare between the foreheads you could have cloned out.  other than that though, i think it''s realy sweet, which is ehanced by its size.  7.</td>', 'you will be punished for the size of the shot, and normally i would be band wagining and telling you to use save to web, or lower quality, or something to make saving it under the kb limit at full size.  but, oddly, the size of the shot for a change adds a degree of intimacy, and there is something tender about it.  i would imagine it would look good in a big frame...  anyway, technically i feel the sun is suffering from some colour abnormality on the left, and there is a bit of glare between the foreheads you could have cloned out.  other than that though, i think it''s realy sweet, which is ehanced by its size.  7.', '2006-07-24 03:44:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(2653691, 368654, 18505, '<td valign="top">I love the feel of this image... I almost wish, however, that you had included a bit more of the long shadows from the tractor and wagon.  Still a lovely, lovely image.. 10</td>', 'I love the feel of this image... I almost wish, however, that you had included a bit more of the long shadows from the tractor and wagon.  Still a lovely, lovely image.. 10', '2006-07-24 03:56:45.000000', NULL, 1),
