(2655181, 365879, 50034, '<td valign="top">Any back story on the markings above "In God We Trust"?  It appears to be "1960" or "196C" &amp; "1980".  This, of course, makes a potential of three dates on the same coin which is a bit confusing, but certainly not your fault!<br/>   "In God We Trust" is a great reminder every time I read it in print.  However, the fact that it is such an innocuous statement of faith that I am truly amazed when someone is offended by it.  When you think about it, every human has a god, even an atheist.  <br/>   God is truly the highest value in a human heart, and the purpose for which every individual finds meaning &amp; defines a successful life.  Most would consider God quite ethereal.  However, I would humbly submit that the atheist''s god is quite corporeal.   (Just a thought!)  :)</td>', 'Any back story on the markings above "In God We Trust"?  It appears to be "1960" or "196C" & "1980".  This, of course, makes a potential of three dates on the same coin which is a bit confusing, but certainly not your fault!   "In God We Trust" is a great reminder every time I read it in print.  However, the fact that it is such an innocuous statement of faith that I am truly amazed when someone is offended by it.  When you think about it, every human has a god, even an atheist.     God is truly the highest value in a human heart, and the purpose for which every individual finds meaning & defines a successful life.  Most would consider God quite ethereal.  However, I would humbly submit that the atheist''s god is quite corporeal.   (Just a thought!)  :)', '2006-07-24 14:08:16.000000', NULL, 1),
