(2658397, 368419, 14671, '<td valign="top">The second time I''ve seen this photo in this challenge but I''m not gonna be a nice cuz its a double.  Its a very crisp and clean image with amazing detail and I can see you took the time to do that but why wouldn''t you take the time to straighten the building???  A 1 or 2 degree CW rotation would have increased the score huge.  I''d also suggested darkening the sky a bit to bring out the gold in the top of the building instead of having it look high key or over contrasted (which haoppens with that color sky).  I might have also use a brightening tool on the trees to bring out the green more to complete the photo.  Well done and good luck in this challenge.  &lt;6&gt;<br/> <br/>Probably would have scored an &lt;8&gt; had the building been straight.  (yes it bothered me that much)</td>', 'The second time I''ve seen this photo in this challenge but I''m not gonna be a nice cuz its a double.  Its a very crisp and clean image with amazing detail and I can see you took the time to do that but why wouldn''t you take the time to straighten the building???  A 1 or 2 degree CW rotation would have increased the score huge.  I''d also suggested darkening the sky a bit to bring out the gold in the top of the building instead of having it look high key or over contrasted (which haoppens with that color sky).  I might have also use a brightening tool on the trees to bring out the green more to complete the photo.  Well done and good luck in this challenge.  <6> Probably would have scored an <8> had the building been straight.  (yes it bothered me that much)', '2006-07-25 12:48:49.000000', NULL, 1),
