(2679165, 367747, 50034, '<td valign="top">Nice recreation of the popular Dream &amp; Poster, <b>Foot Prints</b>.  What a comforting thought to know that even through the periods of my life when <i>"the wind is blowing more than 50 mph winds filled with sand in my face, the sun is beating down on me with unrelenting intensity, my body is weak, and my throat is parched,"</i>  I have confidence that <b>my Best Friend is carrying me!</b> <br/>       I will bookmark this photo as truly one of my favorites!  <b>Thank you for a great photo!</b><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-07-31 12:15:33.</i></td>', 'Nice recreation of the popular Dream & Poster, Foot Prints.  What a comforting thought to know that even through the periods of my life when "the wind is blowing more than 50 mph winds filled with sand in my face, the sun is beating down on me with unrelenting intensity, my body is weak, and my throat is parched,"  I have confidence that my Best Friend is carrying me!        I will bookmark this photo as truly one of my favorites!  Thank you for a great photo!', '2006-07-31 09:14:53.000000', '2006-07-31 13:15:33.000000', 0),
(2679176, 366516, 19959, '<td valign="top">Thanks all for the comments. appreciated.<br/> <br/>I took the shot with my 5D and 70-200 f4 L.<br/>I was looking for close-ups of the poppies but couldn''t gain access to the field (hence the longer lens)<br/> <br/>I''m not sure why I kept the 4x6 aspect, in hindsight this might have looked better in a squarer format.</td>', 'Thanks all for the comments. appreciated. I took the shot with my 5D and 70-200 f4 L.I was looking for close-ups of the poppies but couldn''t gain access to the field (hence the longer lens) I''m not sure why I kept the 4x6 aspect, in hindsight this might have looked better in a squarer format.', '2006-07-31 09:18:00.000000', NULL, 0),
