(2681601, 365769, 30982, '<td valign="top">Trading Post comment<br/> <br/>Yep, I''d have to say it met the challenge!  I know I''ve bought things for a challenge, but never a bottle of liquor (I don''t drink so it''d go to waste.)  Pretty bottle, though!  Well lit, would probably work well as a product ad, though the base is a bit heavy - not sure how you could remedy that except perhaps shoot from above instead of below.  I''m not thrilled with the border - it''s not too heavy for the picture, but it doesn''t add anything for me.</td>', 'Trading Post comment Yep, I''d have to say it met the challenge!  I know I''ve bought things for a challenge, but never a bottle of liquor (I don''t drink so it''d go to waste.)  Pretty bottle, though!  Well lit, would probably work well as a product ad, though the base is a bit heavy - not sure how you could remedy that except perhaps shoot from above instead of below.  I''m not thrilled with the border - it''s not too heavy for the picture, but it doesn''t add anything for me.', '2006-07-31 20:54:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(2681603, 367747, 11518, '<td valign="top">Beautiful shot!  Well deserved Blue!</td>', 'Beautiful shot!  Well deserved Blue!', '2006-07-31 20:54:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(2681646, 368712, 42125, '<td valign="top">Thank you for your comments, they are always in the way to make things better.<br/>About this pictue I think that md8speed is right, i.e. with greater aperture and less speed you would have gained a better depth of field and all the gold would have been in focus.<br/>The way it is now the first thing you look at is the part of the gold that is not in focus. With that fixed I think you would have scored around 6.<br/>The flowers add a lot to the picture and a black background would only make this a picture of a music stand instead of capturing a scene.</td>', 'Thank you for your comments, they are always in the way to make things better.About this pictue I think that md8speed is right, i.e. with greater aperture and less speed you would have gained a better depth of field and all the gold would have been in focus.The way it is now the first thing you look at is the part of the gold that is not in focus. With that fixed I think you would have scored around 6.The flowers add a lot to the picture and a black background would only make this a picture of a music stand instead of capturing a scene.', '2006-07-31 21:16:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(2681699, 367122, 22301, '<td valign="top">Tate, <br/>Thanks for you comment on my on the beach entry and I thought I would return the comment. This is a cool image for gold and makes me want beer. To me it appears that alot of the highlights in the glass appear blown out specifically in the rim of the glass.  I think the composition is great but could see how many people may find it distracting. If I had voted I would have given it a 6, higher if all highlights were there. Thanks again for your comment.<br/>joe</td>', 'Tate, Thanks for you comment on my on the beach entry and I thought I would return the comment. This is a cool image for gold and makes me want beer. To me it appears that alot of the highlights in the glass appear blown out specifically in the rim of the glass.  I think the composition is great but could see how many people may find it distracting. If I had voted I would have given it a 6, higher if all highlights were there. Thanks again for your comment.joe', '2006-07-31 21:38:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(2681700, 367620, 11800, '<td valign="top">A pretty picture! You do pretty, good, young Joey. I like this.</td>', 'A pretty picture! You do pretty, good, young Joey. I like this.', '2006-07-31 21:39:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(2681807, 368188, 57839, '<td valign="top">Fantastic!</td>', 'Fantastic!', '2006-07-31 22:07:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(2681815, 368105, 22301, '<td valign="top">Mark, Thanks for your comment on my on the beach entry and I wish I had got that ribbon too! I thought I would return the comment, congrats on breaking six and having a new personal best. My only suggestion would really be to try a crop where the center of the flower in focus is directly in the intersection of the horizontal and vertical rule of thirds. IMO with so little in focus having the one thing in focus in that spot may have helped out, but really I think its great and thats all I can think of for improvement. THanks again.<br/>joe</td>', 'Mark, Thanks for your comment on my on the beach entry and I wish I had got that ribbon too! I thought I would return the comment, congrats on breaking six and having a new personal best. My only suggestion would really be to try a crop where the center of the flower in focus is directly in the intersection of the horizontal and vertical rule of thirds. IMO with so little in focus having the one thing in focus in that spot may have helped out, but really I think its great and thats all I can think of for improvement. THanks again.joe', '2006-07-31 22:14:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(2681832, 368385, 22301, '<td valign="top">Brent, thanks for the comment my beach entry, thought I would give a comment back. I think like the other commenters the writing on the bucket hurts the photo and I also think that even though you are obvioulsy trying to find gold your score may have been hurt by not having gold in it. But I think the way you composed the shot was well done and good luck next time. Thanks again for the comment.<br/>Joe</td>', 'Brent, thanks for the comment my beach entry, thought I would give a comment back. I think like the other commenters the writing on the bucket hurts the photo and I also think that even though you are obvioulsy trying to find gold your score may have been hurt by not having gold in it. But I think the way you composed the shot was well done and good luck next time. Thanks again for the comment.Joe', '2006-07-31 22:21:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(2681916, 368188, 33361, '<td valign="top">I love this image!</td>', 'I love this image!', '2006-07-31 22:43:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(2681989, 368380, 37779, '<td valign="top">AH! My net has been broken all day and then I get on finally and WAM! RIBBON FOR YOU!!!! HUUUUUUUUUUUUUUUUGE CONGRATS MY FRIEND!!!!!!!</td>', 'AH! My net has been broken all day and then I get on finally and WAM! RIBBON FOR YOU!!!! HUUUUUUUUUUUUUUUUGE CONGRATS MY FRIEND!!!!!!!', '2006-07-31 23:06:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(2682039, 368380, 24613, '<td valign="top">Hi MacKenzie!  I hope you don''t mind that I really don''t like this shot.  This is a personal statement.  But I am amazed at the detail that you went through and the the technical perfection (though nothing''s perfect) of this shot!  The dark is almost "ghostly" dark - GREAT job!  The hair looking "almost" blured, the crisp, clear feel of the face, the hauntingly realistic staples in the face, and those eyes!!  Again, this is not a photo that appeals to me, but I bet if I put this much effort into a shot, I could get a ribbon too.  I didn''t vote on this challenge (shame on me), but I probably would have voted it low. (Shame on us who don''t "REALLY" look at the challenge photos!!!) Since it''s on the "Front Page", I''ve had time to look at it.  Now, I am so very much impressed with your work!  If you nailed the challenge or not is not the issue.  You have used your creativety and your photographic talent to make me, someone who really dosn''t like this shot personnally, to stand up and take notice.  I am extremely impressed with your work! I will be looking for more winners from you!!:) Ray</td>', 'Hi MacKenzie!  I hope you don''t mind that I really don''t like this shot.  This is a personal statement.  But I am amazed at the detail that you went through and the the technical perfection (though nothing''s perfect) of this shot!  The dark is almost "ghostly" dark - GREAT job!  The hair looking "almost" blured, the crisp, clear feel of the face, the hauntingly realistic staples in the face, and those eyes!!  Again, this is not a photo that appeals to me, but I bet if I put this much effort into a shot, I could get a ribbon too.  I didn''t vote on this challenge (shame on me), but I probably would have voted it low. (Shame on us who don''t "REALLY" look at the challenge photos!!!) Since it''s on the "Front Page", I''ve had time to look at it.  Now, I am so very much impressed with your work!  If you nailed the challenge or not is not the issue.  You have used your creativety and your photographic talent to make me, someone who really dosn''t like this shot personnally, to stand up and take notice.  I am extremely impressed with your work! I will be looking for more winners from you!!:) Ray', '2006-07-31 23:23:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(2682113, 368188, 61052, '<td valign="top">HI Manny,<br/> <br/>Congratulations! another ribbon for the master.This image is sensual yet it still is spirited, a great concept. It was a great time you spent with us here during your stay, thank you very much for all the efforts and dedication. Keep it up.</td>', 'HI Manny, Congratulations! another ribbon for the master.This image is sensual yet it still is spirited, a great concept. It was a great time you spent with us here during your stay, thank you very much for all the efforts and dedication. Keep it up.', '2006-07-31 23:43:55.000000', NULL, 0),
