(2688127, 368448, 19670, '<td valign="top">I like the glow around the kids'' heads, and how the bunker shape is repeated by the treeline in the background. Nice shot!</td>', 'I like the glow around the kids'' heads, and how the bunker shape is repeated by the treeline in the background. Nice shot!', '2006-08-02 12:02:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(2688478, 368102, 32754, '<td valign="top">This was just a fantastic idea!  Great smile and wonderful image..well done.</td>', 'This was just a fantastic idea!  Great smile and wonderful image..well done.', '2006-08-02 13:25:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(2688760, 368595, 26045, '<td valign="top">hey, good job bucko!</td>', 'hey, good job bucko!', '2006-08-02 14:39:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(2688862, 368448, 31133, '<td valign="top">Thanks for all the great comments!! Now that I look at it more, I wish I had saturated it heavier, but it is what it is and nothing more or less :-)</td>', 'Thanks for all the great comments!! Now that I look at it more, I wish I had saturated it heavier, but it is what it is and nothing more or less :-)', '2006-08-02 15:07:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(2688977, 368259, 4226, '<td valign="top">** Critique Club **<br/> <br/>Greetings!<br/> <br/>My very first impression was that the image looks very ordinary, its a snapshot look and not a well thought out capture. <br/> <br/>the reason, I think is that the subject is not accentuated in this capture, but its rather mixed up with its surroundings. Also the photo takes away from the moving sense, they you have composed it. its a bit too centered, I would keep some more room on a side to make it more dynamic.<br/> <br/>also since its advanced editing, I think it could benefit from some vignetting. <br/> <br/>if you have any questions regarding this, please feel free to pm me.<br/> <br/>thanks,<br/>Gaurawa<br/> <br/></td>', '** Critique Club ** Greetings! My very first impression was that the image looks very ordinary, its a snapshot look and not a well thought out capture.  the reason, I think is that the subject is not accentuated in this capture, but its rather mixed up with its surroundings. Also the photo takes away from the moving sense, they you have composed it. its a bit too centered, I would keep some more room on a side to make it more dynamic. also since its advanced editing, I think it could benefit from some vignetting.  if you have any questions regarding this, please feel free to pm me. thanks,Gaurawa ', '2006-08-02 15:37:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(2689000, 367687, 4226, '<td valign="top">** Critique Club **<br/> <br/>Greetings!<br/> <br/>Photograph: Well taken, the title is very appropriate and technically, its very well captured.<br/> <br/>Challenge : the challenge was Gold, and I am sure not many people will find enough gold in this picture, there is are more colors in this picture which fight for attention, which I believe is the reason for a lower score. <br/> <br/>Overall, a well taken photograph which doesn''t meet the challenge very well.<br/> <br/>if you have any questions, please feel free to pm me.<br/> <br/>thanks,<br/>Gaurawa</td>', '** Critique Club ** Greetings! Photograph: Well taken, the title is very appropriate and technically, its very well captured. Challenge : the challenge was Gold, and I am sure not many people will find enough gold in this picture, there is are more colors in this picture which fight for attention, which I believe is the reason for a lower score.  Overall, a well taken photograph which doesn''t meet the challenge very well. if you have any questions, please feel free to pm me. thanks,Gaurawa', '2006-08-02 15:44:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(2689059, 368417, 4226, '<td valign="top">** Critique Club **<br/> <br/>Greetings!<br/> <br/>I like the way you have used the lines from the building top. the hue on the gold and sky seems to be off though. the sky has a very dull feel to it. Also the gold can be enhanced with minor color correction edits. <br/> <br/>I don''t think that you can remove the blown out region on left due to sun. To avoid this, you may want to shoot at evening or morning, also that would add to the overall photo by a warm sky tones. <br/> <br/>if you have any questions, feel free to pm me.<br/> <br/>thanks,<br/>Gaurawa</td>', '** Critique Club ** Greetings! I like the way you have used the lines from the building top. the hue on the gold and sky seems to be off though. the sky has a very dull feel to it. Also the gold can be enhanced with minor color correction edits.  I don''t think that you can remove the blown out region on left due to sun. To avoid this, you may want to shoot at evening or morning, also that would add to the overall photo by a warm sky tones.  if you have any questions, feel free to pm me. thanks,Gaurawa', '2006-08-02 16:00:41.000000', NULL, 0),
